{
  "id": "m31l1",
  "title": {
    "es": "Búsqueda",
    "en": "Searching"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Encontrar un elemento"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "La **búsqueda lineal** recorre la lista de principio a fin comparando. Es simple y funciona siempre, pero lenta en listas enormes."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def buscar(lista, x):",
          "    for i, v in enumerate(lista):",
          "        if v == x:",
          "            return i",
          "    return -1",
          "",
          "print(buscar([10, 20, 30], 20))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "1"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "La **búsqueda binaria** es mucho más rápida, pero requiere que la lista esté **ordenada**: descarta la mitad en cada paso."
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Binaria: O(log n) frente a O(n) de la lineal. La diferencia es enorme con millones de datos."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Finding an element"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "**Linear search** scans the list from start to end comparing. Simple and always works, but slow on huge lists."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def buscar(lista, x):",
          "    for i, v in enumerate(lista):",
          "        if v == x:",
          "            return i",
          "    return -1",
          "",
          "print(buscar([10, 20, 30], 20))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "1"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "**Binary search** is much faster, but requires the list to be **sorted**: it discards half at each step."
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Binary: O(log n) vs O(n) for linear. The difference is huge with millions of items."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m31l1e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `busqueda_lineal(lista, x)` que devuelva el índice de `x` o -1 si no está.",
        "en": "Define `busqueda_lineal(lista, x)` returning the index of `x` or -1 if absent."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def busqueda_lineal(lista, x):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def busqueda_lineal(lista, x):",
        "    for i, v in enumerate(lista):",
        "        if v == x:",
        "            return i",
        "    return -1"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Recorre con enumerate y devuelve i al encontrarlo."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Iterate with enumerate and return i on match."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "busqueda_lineal",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  10,
                  20,
                  30
                ],
                20
              ],
              "expected": 1
            },
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  1,
                  2
                ],
                9
              ],
              "expected": -1
            },
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  5
                ],
                5
              ],
              "expected": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m31l1e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `busqueda_binaria(lista, x)` sobre una lista ORDENADA; devuelve el índice o -1.",
        "en": "Define `busqueda_binaria(lista, x)` over a SORTED list; return the index or -1."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def busqueda_binaria(lista, x):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def busqueda_binaria(lista, x):",
        "    lo, hi = 0, len(lista) - 1",
        "    while lo <= hi:",
        "        med = (lo + hi) // 2",
        "        if lista[med] == x:",
        "            return med",
        "        if lista[med] < x:",
        "            lo = med + 1",
        "        else:",
        "            hi = med - 1",
        "    return -1"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Mantén lo y hi; compara con el central y descarta una mitad."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Keep lo and hi; compare with the middle and discard a half."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "busqueda_binaria",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  1,
                  3,
                  5,
                  7,
                  9
                ],
                7
              ],
              "expected": 3
            },
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  1,
                  2,
                  3
                ],
                4
              ],
              "expected": -1
            },
            {
              "args": [
                [
                  1,
                  2,
                  3,
                  4
                ],
                1
              ],
              "expected": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}